   "source": [
    "# Accessing Experiment Data From S3\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook walks through how to access the S3 experiment data in HDF5 format using lazy loaders so that the whole data is not loaded into the RAM.\n",
    "\n",
    "To view your data, edit the `S3Backend` parameters with your `bucket`, `endpoint_url`, and `prefix` values."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e1d3517d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Imports\n",
    "\n",
    "The notebook uses `pd_xray` as backend to perform all the operations. This makes the experience a bit more seamless.\n",
    "\n",
    "For this notebook, we will be using `S3Backend` for the backend and `HDF5Reader` as the file reader. They work together to access the HDF5 files in a lazy manner.\n",
    "\n",
    "Apart from those, `ImageProcessor` can be utilised to process the frames."
   ]
  },
